From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: Standard Dolby Vision through an MCDP2800 LSPCON in level-shifter mode

The Intel NUC7i7BN (Kaby Lake) has no native HDMI: its HDMI socket is a DP
port behind a MegaChips MCDP2800 LSPCON. In PCON mode the MCDP2800 (firmware
1.77) forwards the HDR10 SDP but drops the Dolby VSIF, whichever DIP carries
it, so linux-9950's converter route does not work there. In level-shifter
mode the chip repeats the GPU's own TMDS, so the native-HDMI Dolby Vision
path (DV AVI, Dolby VSIF) reaches the TV.

With DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB set on the LSPCON port's DP connector,
intel_ddi_compute_output_type() returns HDMI and the HDMI compute path
applies. The HDMI enable path switches the LSPCON to level-shifter mode
through the standard dual-mode register over the AUX DDC
(intel_lspcon_set_ls_dv()); the disable path switches it back to PCON mode.
Without DV the port is the usual PCON-mode DP connector (4K60, HDR10). The
port's intel_hdmi takes the DP connector, with dual-mode type LSPCON and a
340 MHz TMDS limit: DV on this route is 4K up to 30 Hz. The shared link
policy admits the route through verified_bridge (native_hdmi stays false on
an LSPCON port); all other link guards apply. The DP connector caches the
sink's Dolby caps from its EDID, as the HDMI connector does.

While in level-shifter mode the LSPCON does not answer native AUX: DP detect
reports the HPD state only and keeps the EDID, short HPD pulses and DP link
checks are skipped, and intel_lspcon_resume() leaves the chip alone. The
connector HW state check accepts an HDMI-mode DDI on that DP connector, and
the port's InfoFrame hooks use the GPU's DIPs for the HDMI-mode output and
the LSPCON hooks otherwise.

Eligibility: i915.dv_lspcon (-1 = DMI-allowlisted boards [NUC7i7BNB], the
default; 0 = off; 1 = any gen9/10 LSPCON port), and at modeset a MegaChips
MC2800 with an allowlisted firmware (1.77).

Hardware evidence: NUC Display Lab (nuc-hardware-lab v0.3.1/v0.4.0-dvlab,
reports #15 and #17), NUC7i7BNB, MCDP2800 HW 2.2 FW 1.77, LG OLED55C3,
4K23.976 RGB8: Dolby Vision logo and the correct picture from the RGB8
tunnel, a no-VSIF control shows the raw tunnel, and a metadata-only A/B pair
renders darker/brighter. That lab switched modes by re-probing i915; the
in-modeset switch of this patch is compile-tested only, not yet verified on
hardware. Ported from LibreELEC-yblod linux-9931 (Linux 7.3) to Linux 7.2.6.
Applies after linux-9950.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -775,7 +775,11 @@ bool intel_ddi_connector_get_hw_state(struct intel_connector *intel_connector)
 
 	if (ddi_mode == TRANS_DDI_MODE_SELECT_HDMI ||
 	    ddi_mode == TRANS_DDI_MODE_SELECT_DVI) {
-		ret = type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA;
+		/* linux-9951: the LSPCON level-shifter DV output is an HDMI-mode
+		 * DDI behind the DP connector. */
+		ret = type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA ||
+			(type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort &&
+			 intel_dp_lspcon_dv_allowed(enc_to_dig_port(encoder)));
 	} else if (ddi_mode == TRANS_DDI_MODE_SELECT_FDI_OR_128B132B && !HAS_DP20(display)) {
 		ret = type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_VGA;
 	} else if (ddi_mode == TRANS_DDI_MODE_SELECT_DP_SST) {
@@ -2986,6 +2990,10 @@ static void intel_ddi_pre_enable_hdmi(struct intel_atomic_state *state,
 	struct intel_digital_port *dig_port = enc_to_dig_port(encoder);
 	struct intel_hdmi *intel_hdmi = &dig_port->hdmi;
 
+	/* linux-9951: Dolby Vision through the LSPCON in level-shifter mode. */
+	if (intel_dp_lspcon_dv_allowed(dig_port))
+		intel_lspcon_set_ls_dv(dig_port, true);
+
 	intel_dp_dual_mode_set_tmds_output(intel_hdmi, true);
 	intel_ddi_enable_clock(encoder, crtc_state);
 
@@ -3216,6 +3224,10 @@ static void intel_ddi_post_disable_hdmi(struct intel_atomic_state *state,
 	intel_ddi_disable_clock(encoder);
 
 	intel_dp_dual_mode_set_tmds_output(intel_hdmi, false);
+
+	/* linux-9951: back to PCON mode for the DP connector's usual output. */
+	if (intel_dp_lspcon_dv_allowed(dig_port))
+		intel_lspcon_set_ls_dv(dig_port, false);
 }
 
 static void intel_ddi_post_disable_hdmi_or_sst(struct intel_atomic_state *state,
@@ -4478,6 +4490,11 @@ intel_ddi_compute_output_type(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP:
 		return INTEL_OUTPUT_EDP;
 	case DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort:
+		/* linux-9951: Dolby Vision on an LSPCON port is an HDMI-mode
+		 * output with the LSPCON in level-shifter mode. */
+		if (to_intel_digital_connector_state(conn_state)->dv_lab_standard &&
+		    intel_dp_lspcon_dv_allowed(enc_to_dig_port(encoder)))
+			return INTEL_OUTPUT_HDMI;
 		return INTEL_OUTPUT_DP;
 	default:
 		MISSING_CASE(conn_state->connector->connector_type);
